FINAL5  THE DECISIVE MEASUREMENT: is the fixed column Sigma_gas = a0/(pi G x_b^2) there?
Criteria committed alone, before this script and before any number. Footings never pooled.
kappa = 1/2 FITTED; not theory closed. Adopts nothing.

x_b^2 = R_b(1+R_b) = 5.41 x 6.41 = 34.6781;   x_b = 5.888811

## KA1  the required column (both footings, SI then astrophysical)
  canonical:  Sigma_gas = a0/(pi G x_b^2) = 1.287355e-02 kg/m^2 = 6.1627 Msun/pc^2 = 6.1627e+12 Msun/Mpc^2
  alt      :  Sigma_gas = a0/(pi G x_b^2) = 1.555779e-02 kg/m^2 = 7.4477 Msun/pc^2 = 7.4477e+12 Msun/Mpc^2
  -> reproduces GAS1's 6.1627 / 7.4477 Msun/pc^2 to <1e-3   [KA1 PASS]

## KA2  the prediction restated: g_bar is a CONSTANT at these radii
     g_bar(R) = G M_bar(<R)/R^2 = G (pi R^2 Sigma_gas)/R^2 = pi G Sigma_gas = a0/x_b^2

  canonical:  g_bar = 2.699196e-12 m/s^2  =  a0/34.678  =  0.02699 x 1e-10 m/s^2   (a0/x_b^2 = 2.699196e-12, ratio 1.000000000000)
  alt      :  g_bar = 3.262001e-12 m/s^2  =  a0/34.678  =  0.03262 x 1e-10 m/s^2   (a0/x_b^2 = 3.262001e-12, ratio 1.000000000000)
  -> exact to 1e-12, both footings   [KA2 PASS]

