## KA4 / KA5  the implied density, and the amplitude in each observable

PROFILE A = the required sheet.  M(<R) = pi R^2 Sigma_gas  =>  rho = Sigma_gas/(2R),  rho ~ R^-1.
PROFILE B = a plausible hot halo. rho ~ R^-2 (the beta ~ 2/3 / outer r^-2 behaviour measured in
            groups and clusters), normalised to the SAME local density at R_ref = 1 Mpc.

  cosmic means used below (ON DISK): rho_b = 6.205e+09, rho_m = 3.975e+10 Msun/Mpc^3

### PROFILE A  --  density and electron column

| R (Mpc) | rho [kg/m^3] | rho [Msun/Mpc^3] | n_e [cm^-3] | N_e sheet [cm^-2] | N_e sph(2.6) [cm^-2] |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 0.3 | 6.953e-25 | 1.027e+13 | 3.647e-04 | 6.752e+20 | 1.924e+21 |
| 1.0 | 2.086e-25 | 3.081e+12 | 1.094e-04 | 6.752e+20 | 1.087e+21 |
| 2.0 | 1.043e-25 | 1.541e+12 | 5.470e-05 | 6.752e+20 | 5.107e+20 |
| 2.6 | 8.023e-26 | 1.185e+12 | 4.208e-05 | 0.000e+00 | 0.000e+00 |

  N_e sheet   = Sigma_gas/(mu_e m_p): the uniform projected sheet, FLAT in b (the minimum).
  N_e sph     = that times arccosh(R_out/b): the spherical rho~R^-1 reading, cut at R_out = 2.6 Mpc.
  Either way the bracket is a factor <= 2.9; the plateau is FLAT or nearly so over 0.3 -> 2 Mpc.

  KA5: the analytic emission measure (arccosh/b closed form) matches brute-force quadrature
       at all radii inside R_out   [KA5 PASS]

