## Detectability with the ACT DR6 y map (ON DISK)

  Noise basis, ON DISK not memory: GO1's own measured stacked y error
    sigma(M_gas^y) = 6.9e12 Msun, shell 1 -> 2.83 R500 (aperture radius 1.868 Mpc), N = 102, z = 0.143
    [go1.json: primary/full/sig_at/2.83/Gy].  sigma(mean y) ~ sqrt(Omega_ap)/sqrt(N).

    that aperture subtends theta = 11.95 arcmin  ->  Omega = 448.8 arcmin^2
    ACT DR6 beam (FETCH_LOG.md, ON DISK) = 1.6 arcmin FWHM -> Omega_beam = 2.90 arcmin^2

  For a FLAT column the enclosed gas mass in a cylinder of radius R is  pi R^2 Sigma_gas, so the
  1-sigma error on the COLUMN is just the error on the aperture gas mass divided by pi R^2 --
  no temperature, no geometry factor, no clumping.  GO1's printed error therefore reads directly
  as a column error:

    sigma(Sigma)  =  6.9e12 / (pi x 1.868^2)  =  6.294e+11 Msun/Mpc^2  =  0.102 x Sigma_gas   (1 sigma, N = 102, aperture 1.868 Mpc)

  That is the whole measurement.  Scaling to P1 (N = 17335) and to aperture radius R, with
  sigma(Sigma) ~ 1/(theta_ap sqrt(N)):

| R (Mpc) | theta @z=.308 (') | beams in aperture | sigma(Sigma)/Sigma_gas | y pred @0.2 keV | S/N if the column is real |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 0.3 | 1.06 | 1.2 | 0.0879 | 1.758e-07 | 11 |
| 1.0 | 3.55 | 13.6 | 0.0264 | 1.758e-07 | 38 |
| 2.0 | 7.10 | 54.6 | 0.0132 | 1.758e-07 | 76 |
| 2.6 | 9.23 | 92.3 | 0.0101 | 0.000e+00 | 99 |

  So a straight stack of the 17,335 P1 lenses on the ACT map already on disk measures the
  projected gas column at 0.3 - 2.6 Mpc to about ONE PER CENT of the required value.  If the
  column is there, this is a ~100 sigma detection.  If it is not, the reading is dead by the same
  factor.  There is no regime in which the experiment is merely suggestive.

  CAVEAT (carried as a bracket, B7): Sigma_meas ~ 1/T_model.  Doubling the assumed temperature
  halves the inferred column, i.e. halves f_col.  The decision rule is therefore evaluated at
  kT = 0.1 / 0.2 / 0.5 keV and the label must agree at all three.

  Beam check (ACT 1.6' FWHM, at z = 0.308, spherical rho ~ R^-1 reading):

| R (Mpc) | theta (') | y intrinsic | y beam-smeared | smeared/intrinsic |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 0.3 | 1.06 | 5.001e-07 | 4.600e-07 | 0.92 |
| 1.0 | 3.55 | 2.838e-07 | 2.796e-07 | 0.99 |
| 2.0 | 7.10 | 1.322e-07 | 1.288e-07 | 0.97 |
| 2.6 | 9.23 | 0.000e+00 | 2.557e-08 | inf |

  -> at 0.3 Mpc (1.06') the beam suppresses the intrinsic signal by the factor shown;
     the pre-registered fix is to grade the 0.3 Mpc point on the lowest-redshift third of P1.

