| x = r/R500 | R (Mpc) | required, canon (Msun) | GO1 measured y-gas (Msun) | f_col | shortfall |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 2.83 | 1.87 | 6.746e+13 | 1.26e+13 +- 6.9e+12 | 0.187 | +8.0 sigma |
| 4.00 | 2.64 | 1.349e+14 | 2.20e+13 +- 1.7e+13 | 0.163 | +6.6 sigma |
| 5.66 | 3.74 | 2.701e+14 | 6.00e+12 +- 2.6e+13 | 0.022 | +10.2 sigma |
| 8.00 | 5.28 | 5.397e+14 | -4.00e+12 +- 5.1e+13 | -0.007 | +10.7 sigma |
| 11.30 | 7.46 | 1.077e+15 | 7.70e+13 +- 7.5e+13 | 0.072 | +13.3 sigma |

  These are GROUPS (M500 ~ 1e14, ~10x an L* halo) -- they should carry MORE gas than an L* galaxy,
  not less.  They supply f_col = 0.19 +- 0.10 of the requirement at 1.87 Mpc and are in deficit at
  +8.0 to +13.3 sigma.  Because the requirement is mass-independent while the available gas scales with
  halo mass, moving to the 17,335 ISOLATED L* lenses can only push f_col further down.

