## The check that needs no new data at all: does the required gas fit in the halo?

  L* halo mass used for scale only: M200 = 1.2e+12 Msun  [memory -- quoted for context]

| R (Mpc) | M_gas,req canon (Msun) | M_gas,req / M200 | verdict |
|---|---|---|---|
| 0.3 | 1.658e+12 | 1.4 | IMPOSSIBLE |
| 1.0 | 1.928e+13 | 16.1 | IMPOSSIBLE |
| 2.0 | 7.736e+13 | 64.5 | IMPOSSIBLE |
| 2.6 | 1.308e+14 | 109.0 | IMPOSSIBLE |

  A halo can only hold Omega_b/Omega_m x M200 ~ 0.16 M200 of baryons in total.  The reading
  demands tens to hundreds of times that, in gas alone, inside the same radius.  No instrument
  systematic has to be modelled to see this: it is a mass-conservation statement.

### X-ray: total luminosity and observed flux of the required sheet (canonical, kT = 0.2 keV)

| R_out (Mpc) | L_X 0.5-2keV (erg/s) | F_X @ z=0.308 (erg/s/cm^2) |
|---|---|---|
| 1.0 | 1.149e+44 | 3.497e-09 |
| 2.0 | 2.297e+44 | 6.994e-09 |
| 2.6 | 2.986e+44 | 9.092e-09 |

  For scale: real isolated L* galaxies have diffuse L_X(0.5-2 keV) ~ 1e39-1e41 erg/s
  [memory].  The reading requires ~1e44-3e44 erg/s from EVERY one of them, i.e. a rich-cluster
  X-ray luminosity in a galaxy that X-ray surveys have looked at and not seen.

### Data volume for the X-ray leg (derived from GO1/DATA_PLAN.md tile sizes, ON DISK)

  mean event tile = 14.5 MB over 10.67 deg^2 unique -> 1.36 MB/deg^2
  KiDS-1000 footprint = 1000 deg^2  ->  events 1.36 GB
  exposure maps ~ 32 MB per band per tile -> 3.00 GB for one band over 1000 deg^2
  (GO1 priced 0.73 GB for 11 groups; the full KiDS lens stack costs roughly 2 GB of events.
   eRASS1 depth 80-210 s is enough for a 17,000-object STACK, not for any single system.)

## The pre-registered decision rule, evaluated on the EXISTING group-scale measurement

    nearest tabulated large-scale radius is GO1's x = 2.83 (R = 1.868 Mpc):
      f_col = 0.187 +- 0.102
      -> NO VERDICT [0.10 < f_col < 0.50, or significance < 3 sigma]

  So the group-scale data already point the same way but are NOT yet inside the frozen kill region;
  the run to do is P1 (17,335 isolated L* lenses), where the requirement is identical and the
  supply is smaller by roughly the halo-mass ratio.

